findings.suggestedFix:
Move `this._warnedUnannounceable = true` above the programmatic check so it executes regardless of the outcome:

```js
_warnUnannounceable() {
  if (this._warnedUnannounceable) return
  this._warnedUnannounceable = true
  if (
    this.triggerWrapper &&
    this.triggerWrapper.hasAttribute("data-combobox-trigger-programmatic")
  ) {
    return
  }
  console.warn(...)
}
```

Poll for the absence with a bounded timeout, e.g.:
```ts
// Give the programmatic hook ample time to mount and (incorrectly) warn.
await page.waitForTimeout(500);
expect(warnings.filter(w => w.includes("#programmatic-combobox:"))).toHaveLength(0);
```
Or use `expect.poll` with a `.toBe(0)` after a fixed delay.
